<main class="legal-stage">
<div class="legal-card">
<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
<p class="legal-updated">Last updated: January 2026</p>
<p>
        These terms cover bookings made through <strong>gedionmutua.com</strong> for 1:1 sessions
        with Gedion Mutua. By booking a session, you agree to the terms below.
      </p>
<h2>Booking &amp; payment</h2>
<ul>
<li>Sessions are billed at $15 / hour (≈ KES 2,000), payable via M-Pesa.</li>
<li>Payment is confirmed manually: you send the M-Pesa payment, then submit your
          confirmation name and code, which is verified on WhatsApp before the session is
          confirmed.</li>
<li>A session is only considered booked once payment has been verified and confirmed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Cancellations &amp; rescheduling</h2>
<ul>
<li>You can reschedule a session at no extra cost with at least 24 hours' notice, by
          messaging on WhatsApp.</li>
<li>Cancellations made less than 24 hours before the session may not be eligible for a
          refund.</li>
<li>If Gedion needs to cancel or reschedule, you'll be offered a new time or a full refund.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Refunds</h2>
<ul>
<li>Refunds for eligible cancellations are issued to the M-Pesa number the payment was sent
          from, within 3–5 business days.</li>
<li>Payments that can't be verified (wrong code, mismatched name, etc.) will be followed up
          on WhatsApp before any refund decision is made.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Liability</h2>
<p>
        Sessions are provided on a best-effort, advisory basis. They do not constitute formal
        financial, legal, or engineering certification unless explicitly agreed in writing.
      </p>
<h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>
        These terms may be updated from time to time. The current version will always be available
        at this page.
      </p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or
        on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gedion-mutua-841481100/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
